[39;49m[K[2m• [22mA terminal emulator is an app that gives you a text-based window for talking[39m[49m[0m
[39;49m[K  to a computer. It lets you type commands, run programs, and see their output[39m[49m[0m
[39;49m[K  without using a graphical interface. The emulator itself does not usually do[39m[49m[0m
[39;49m[K  the work; it connects your keyboard and screen to a shell or another command-[39m[49m[0m
[39;49m[K  line program. It also handles things like text display, colors, cursor[39m[49m[0m
[39;49m[K  movement, scrolling, and keyboard shortcuts. Developers and system[39m[49m[0m
[39;49m[K  administrators use terminal emulators to manage files, install tools, run[39m[49m[0m
[39;49m[K  scripts, connect to servers, and inspect what software is doing. In simple[39m[49m[0m
[39;49m[K  terms, it is a modern software version of an old physical terminal, letting[39m[49m[0m
[39;49m[K  you control a computer through typed commands.[39m[49m[0m[r[19;3H[20;2H[0m[49m[K[21;2H[0m[49m[K[22;34H[0m[49m[K[23;2H[0m[49m[K[39m[49m[0m[0 q[?25h[22;3H[?2026l[?2026h[20;2H[0m[49m[K[21;2H[0m[49m[K[22;34H[0m[49m[K[23;2H[0m[49m[K[39m[49m[0m[0 q[?25h[22;3H[?2026l]0;agent-bridge-record-4...[?2026h[20;2H[0m[49m[K[21;2H[0m[49m[K[22;34H[0m[49m[K[23;2H[0m[49m[K[39m[49m[0m[0 q[?25h[22;3H[?2026l[?2026h[20;2H[0m[49m[K[21;2H[0m[49m[K[22;8H[0m[49m[K[23;2H[0m[49m[K[24;20H[0m[49m[K[22;3H/quit[24;3H[1m[38;5;6;49m/quit  exit Codex[39m[49m[0m[0 q[?25h[22;8H[?2026l[?2026h[20;1H[J[20;2H[0m[49m[K[21;2H[0m[49m[K[22;19H[0m[49m[K[23;2H[0m[49m[K[22;1H[2m›[22;3HShutting down...[39m[49m[0m[?25l[?2026l[20;1H[J]0;[<1u[<u[>4;0m[?2004l[?1004l[0 q[?25h[0 q[?25hToken usage: total=5,300 input=5,160 (+ 9,600 cached) output=140
